<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Matilda of England, Duchess of Saxony</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1156–<a href="/years/1189">1189</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Matilda of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> was the eldest daughter of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-ii-of-england">Henry II of England</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eleanor-of-aquitaine">Eleanor of Aquitaine</a>. In 1168 she married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-saxony">Duke of Saxony</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bavaria">Bavaria</a>, and lived at his court in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, where she was a patron of literature. After Henry was deposed in 1180 she accompanied him into exile at her father's court. Their son Otto IV became <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-roman-emperor">Holy Roman Emperor</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/matilda-of-england-duchess-of-saxony.jpg" alt="Matilda of England, Duchess of Saxony" width="320" height="796" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Helmarshausen Benedictine monastery · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Matildaofengland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
